__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
.obsidian/workspace*.json
.obsidian/cache
# local-only art sources (hi-res / third-party packs kept out of the repo)
assets/srcart/
assets/icons/
assets/gameicons_svg/
assets/gameicons/
# docs/data/ is a mixed directory — see CLAUDE.md's "What may be committed"
# (the line is verbatim vs derived, not third-party vs ours). Default is
# ignore-everything (the compiled card DB is verbatim printed card text:
# index.json, scenarios/, players/, rules.json — plus the rasterized icon
# masks in icons.json), with an explicit allow-list of derived files below.
docs/data/*
# ...except our own summarized stage tips (tools/build_tips.py writes only
# text this project wrote itself; nothing is reproduced verbatim). Committed
# so the Pages build doesn't re-scrape a third-party site on every deploy.
!docs/data/tips.json
# Hall of Beorn raw per-scenario API responses (verbatim third-party card
# data) — never committed. The *aggregated* output built from them,
# tools/data/enrichment.json, is just a per-scenario list of encounter-set
# names and IS committed — see tools/build_hob_enrichment.py.
tools/data/hob_cache/
# Vision of the Palantir strategy-tip HTML cache (verbatim third-party page
# content; never committed — see tools/build_tips.py). Its summarized
# output, docs/data/tips.json, is allow-listed above.
tools/data/tips_cache/
# The same articles converted to readable markdown by
# tools/build_votp_corpus.py (narrowed to `div.entry-content`). Lives in the
# vault (the repo root is an Obsidian vault) so it can be read alongside
# quests/ and design/ — but it is still verbatim third-party prose, so it is
# a local research corpus only: never committed, never shipped. Only text we
# write ourselves from reading it reaches docs/data/tips.json.
research/votp/
# Warriors of the West blog posts, the SECOND tip-distillation source
# (tools/build_wotw_corpus.py) - mostly Nightmare reviews and turn-by-turn
# reports, so it covers the mode Vision of the Palantir barely touches. Same
# posture and same reason as the two above: verbatim third-party prose, a
# local research corpus only, never committed and never shipped. Only text we
# write ourselves from reading it reaches tools/data/tips_distilled.json.
tools/data/wotw_cache/
research/wotw/
# Raw upstream font headers fetched by tools/build_fonts.py. The DERIVED
# output, tools/data/fonts.json, IS committed (glyph masks + widths, MIT via
# pimoroni/pimoroni-pico — see NOTICE): it is small, its licence permits
# redistribution, and the alternative is a network fetch in CI, which the
# data policy calls a smell. The .hpp sources themselves are just build
# input and are re-fetchable from the pin.
tools/data/fonts_cache/
# Official FFG rulebooks parsed to markdown by tools/build_rules_corpus.py,
# and indexed by qmd for semantic search (collection `lotr-lcg-rules`). Same
# posture and the same reason as research/votp/ above: this is verbatim FFG
# rules text, so it is a local research corpus only. Only summaries we write
# ourselves — rules/*.md — are committed. See rules/README.md.
research/rules/

# Design-pane render output (tools/build_design_pane.py). Build artifact:
# every image in it is regenerated from tests/scenes.py.
build/
